## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

Undelivered inbox content is carried across a same-alias session re-register only in memory. InMemoryRelay.register, when the existing lease is alive under a different session_id, moves the old keys undelivered messages to the new key (relay.ml:782-790). SqliteRelay.register (2681-2722) has no equivalent: after a session restart re-registers the alias under a new session id, mail that arrived while the session was down sits under the old (node_id, session_id), unreachable (poll reads the new leases key), and the gc loops stale-inbox sweep (relay.ml:3200-3221, every 300s) destroys it. Mail sent during a restart is delivered after re-register in the test world and silently deleted on prod.

## Fix direction

Mirror the move in sqlite register (copy inboxes rows from the old key to the new one inside the upsert path), or make the inbox key alias-scoped.

## Evidence

Server-core review 2026-09-17.